# A step that writes a table and reads it back, and hands on what it read: the read is of the table as `keep` left it,
# inside the step, so the table keeps what `keep` leaves there, in the codomain (rule 4, as `readback-one-body`);
# what was read goes back to `main`, which prints it. The library's operations whose result the body names are steps:
# `let con = Connection::open(..)`, `let stored = con.prepare(..)?.query_map(..)?.collect::<..>()?`, which `con`
# goes into through the calls it runs on.

route ledger.main
step main/Ledger()
step main/Ledger.keep
step main/Ledger.keep/open
step main/Ledger.keep/collect   # H

line entry > main call
line main/Ledger() > Ledger·ledger@main/Ledger() value
known #126 line Ledger·ledger@main/Ledger() > main/Ledger.keep value   # the body uses the instance itself, and a step inside takes it too
line main/Ledger.keep > Ledger·ledger@main/Ledger.keep value     # `&mut self`: keep changes the ledger
line main/Ledger.keep/open > _·con@main/Ledger.keep/open value
line Ledger·ledger@main/Ledger() > main/Ledger.keep/open value   # K
line _·con@main/Ledger.keep/open > main/Ledger.keep/collect value   # H
line _·con@main/Ledger.keep/open > main/Ledger.keep value   # keep's own `con.execute`
line main/Ledger.keep/collect > _·stored@main/Ledger.keep/collect value   # H
line _·stored@main/Ledger.keep/collect > main/Ledger.keep value   # H: keep hands it back
line main/Ledger.keep > SQLite(notes) own
line main/Ledger.keep > main back  # the notes read back, a Vec<String>
line main > Screen own

home Ledger·ledger@main/Ledger() main
home Ledger·ledger@main/Ledger.keep main
home _·con@main/Ledger.keep/open main/Ledger.keep
home _·stored@main/Ledger.keep/collect main/Ledger.keep   # H

# An error is a value (#138): `?` hands on what a step fails with, converted to the function's error type, here no type
# of the code's (`io::Error`, `rusqlite::Error`); each border it crosses uncaught hands it on. An opened step takes what
# its steps hand on, which Atlas does not draw for an error of no type of the code's.
line main/Ledger.keep > _@main/Ledger.keep value
line main/Ledger.keep/collect > _@main/Ledger.keep/collect value
line main/Ledger.keep/open > _@main/Ledger.keep/open value
known #138 line _@main/Ledger.keep/collect > main/Ledger.keep value
known #138 line _@main/Ledger.keep/open > main/Ledger.keep value
home _@main/Ledger.keep main
home _@main/Ledger.keep/collect main/Ledger.keep
home _@main/Ledger.keep/open main/Ledger.keep

side entry left
side SQLite(notes) right
side Screen right

# H: a method call with a turbofish (`.collect::<T>()`) whose result the body names is no step (without the turbofish
#    it is one, handed `con`).
# K: a value handed through a field reaches no step inside: `Connection::open(&self.path)` hands `self` (#121,
#    decision 1, cause 3: the reader's `held_in` skips `self` even inside an argument)
